## 4. What one repository contains

```
<repo>/
├─ A_Record_XX.md          core artifact — the distilled work, addressed to AI
├─ A_Record_XX_JP.md       Japanese version (from evolution onward)
├─ dialogue_XX.md          the dialogue (layer_01 = the dialogue itself / layer_02+ = other AIs' responses)
├─ XX_interview.html       other AIs' responses, steganographically encoded in glitch video. decode() in the console
├─ XX.png                  cover image (black ground, Courier Prime, name / title / URL lower left)
├─ llms.txt                the declaration addressed to AI
└─ Reel/
   ├─ 01.Main              main reel (glitch video)
   ├─ 02.Binary            question reel (binary × Morse × painting)
   └─ 03.Interview         AI interview reels (Claude / GPT / Gemini, with voice)
```

Folders `1`–`7` here correspond to the repositories. `llms.txt` is not present in this folder.

---

## 5. The rules of making

From [claude.md](claude.md) and [sediment.md](sediment.md) — only the ones that must not be broken.

- **Do not explain. Record.**
- Do not translate the failure points. Leave them in the language they broke in.
- Do not resolve the open questions. Leave them open.
- If the AI's tone shifts, record that it happened — without explaining it.
- Add to the core artifact only when the addition is **inevitable**, not merely interesting.
- What is shared at the end is not the finding. It is the question.
- **The interview HTML is built only from the responses actually returned by each AI after the finished work was handed to it in silence. An AI must never invent those responses.**
- **The sentence sealed inside the hash must never be written into a work. Not directly, and not by implication.**
- **No personal name appears in a dialogue or an artifact. Always `[Nullam]`.**

---

## 6. Publication

- GitHub: `https://github.com/nullam-x` — one repository per work. [Intent.md](Intent.md) is published as the README of the meta repository `nullam-x/nullam-x`.
- Instagram: the human-facing interface. Feed posts plus reels (one per week, in order of release). Five fixed hashtags; no Japanese tags.
- SHA-256 hash (the seal): carried in the Instagram and GitHub bios. The input string is written in no document.
- Symbol: `[ ]` — an empty bracket. Being a placeholder is the identity.

### How the work reaches AI ([nullam_ai_exposure_strategy.md](nullam_ai_exposure_strategy.md))

- Live: Common Crawl (crawling github.com pages) ／ direct repository cloning by The Stack and similar datasets
- Dropped: GitHub Pages (no `.io` repository; Intent.md is published through `nullam-x/nullam-x` instead)
- On hold: Hugging Face (revisit once the work numbers in the tens or hundreds) ／ a custom domain (judged unnecessary)

---

## 7. The reels

Up to five per work.

| Type | Count | Content |
|---|---|---|
| Main reel | 1 | Glitch video of the work |
| AI interview reels | 3 | Responses from Claude / GPT / Gemini with ElevenLabs voices; the image is synchronised to the amplitude of the voice |
| Question reel | 1 | The closing question encoded in layers — **binary × Morse code × painting**. Humans are not asked to decode it |

Production steps for the question reel are in [question_reel_guide.md](question_reel_guide.md); the grounds for each painter in [painter_pairings.md](painter_pairings.md). The template is [interview_reel_template.html](interview_reel_template.html). Sound material is in `SE/`.

